                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\Sigma)
            %li
              %p
                In particular, the
                %strong Lebesgue-measurable
                sets in the real line are the elements of the completion of the Borel
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lebesgue+measure"} Lebesgue measure
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToVonNeumannAlgebras Relation to von Neumann algebras
          %p
            One version of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gelfand+duality"} Gelfand duality theorem
            states that the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative
            = succeed "-" do
